# Battery prices since 1991: true or myth?
subtitle: "Four claims about lithium-ion batteries, true or myth? Two hosts argue each one, then the price of an electric car's battery in 1991."
tags: ["economics","data"]
format: quiz
thumb: "band \"Ten times cheaper? Not even close\" stamp \"MYTH?\""

## Battery prices since 1991: true or myth?
feedback:
    style: dry
    perfect: You could run a battery factory.
    good: Sharper than our co-host.
    poor: Batteries fool almost everyone.
    none: The myths had a full charge today.
affirm: playful
sources:
    - id: owid
      title: Battery costs have declined by 99% in the last three decades, making electrified transport a reality
      authors: Hannah Ritchie and Pablo Rosado (Our World in Data)
      year: 2026
      url: https://ourworldindata.org/battery-price-decline
      finding: lithium-ion cells cost about $9,200 per kWh in 1991 and $78 in 2024, a fall of more than 99%; cumulative production grew 27 million-fold 1991–2023; the cells in a standard electric car cost around $5,000 today and would have cost over $20,000 a decade earlier
    - id: zt
      title: Re-examining rates of lithium-ion battery technology improvement and cost decline
      authors: M. S. Ziegler and J. E. Trancik
      year: 2021
      finding: the price of lithium-ion cells fell about 97% from 1991 to 2018

    sequence claims at.y 455 size 270 items [{"icon":{"of":"battery","set":"twemoji"},"label":"10× cheaper?","mark":{"text":"Myth","color":"#b5482e"}},{"icon":{"of":"factory","set":"twemoji"},"label":"Cheaper by making more?","mark":{"text":"True","color":"#2f6b8f"}},{"icon":{"of":"snail","set":"twemoji"},"label":"Fastest fall: 1990s?","mark":{"text":"Myth","color":"#b5482e"}},{"icon":{"of":"automobile","set":"twemoji"},"label":"Car cells: $5,000?","mark":{"text":"True","color":"#2f6b8f"}}] show_upcoming dots hidden true
    icon car size 280 set twemoji x 220 y 430 icon_look picture of automobile hidden true
    text k1991 "1991: $600,000" #b5482e x 640 y 480 font_size 64 hidden true
    text know "today: $5,000" #2f6b8f cites ["owid"] x 640 y 370 font_size 64 hidden true

    card title "Batteries since 1991: true or myth?"

A: How much cheaper have lithium-ion batteries, the ones in our phones and cars, become since 1991? Four claims: true or myth?
    draw claims_dot_1 claims_dot_2 claims_dot_3 claims_dot_4 parallel true

B: First: they're about ten times cheaper than in 1991. Sounds right to me.
    draw claims_1

    quiz "Lithium-ion batteries are about ten times cheaper than in 1991. True or myth?" on_canvas true reveal.text "MYTH: 100×+" reveal.at.x 790 reveal.at.y 540 reveal.size 40
        right: Myth: more than a hundred times cheaper, from about nine thousand two hundred dollars per kilowatt-hour in 1991 to seventy-eight in 2024.
        * True
        + Myth

B: Fine. Second: they got cheaper because we made so many of them.
    draw claims_2

    quiz "Batteries got cheaper mainly because the world made more of them. True or myth?" on_canvas true reveal.text "TRUE: ×27M" reveal.at.x 790 reveal.at.y 540 reveal.size 40
        right: True. Production grew twenty-seven million times, and the more the world made, the cheaper each one got.
        + True
        * Myth

B: Then the price must have crashed fastest at the start, in the early nineties.
    draw claims_3

    quiz "Battery prices fell fastest in the early 1990s. True or myth?" on_canvas true reveal.text "MYTH: slow start" reveal.at.x 790 reveal.at.y 540 reveal.size 40
        right: Myth. The early years were slow: the market was tiny, and one company, Sony, held most of the technology.
        * True
        + Myth

B: Last one: the battery cells in an electric car cost about five thousand dollars today.
    draw claims_4

    quiz "The battery cells in a standard electric car cost about $5,000 today. True or myth?" on_canvas true reveal.text "TRUE: ~$5,000" reveal.at.x 790 reveal.at.y 540 reveal.size 40
        right: True. Only ten years ago, the same cells cost over twenty thousand.
        + True
        * Myth

B: You got {score} of {score_total}. So what would my car's battery have cost in 1991?
    draw claims_strip

    erase claims claims_strip claims_1_mark claims_2_mark claims_3_mark claims_4_mark

A: Close to si (@draw car k1991 know@)x hundred thousand dollars, more than the car itself. That's what a ninety-nine percent fall buys you.

